  "question": {
    "text": "The potential energy of a particle under a conservative force is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.&nbsp;The equilibrium position of the particle is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;will be"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math><br />For a conservative field, Force, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br />At equilibrium position, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>·</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></math>"
  }
